  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Show error for `-X lua_script` if no Lua support",
  "description": "Wireshark/tshark may be built without Lua support.* This patch adds an error message if the user specifies the `-X lua_script` command-line argument to a program built without Lua support, so the user is not left wondering why their script isn't working.\n\n\\* This is set to become an issue again on CentOS 8, since the official wireshark RPMs do not have lua support. (Wireshark requires Lua 5.1/5.2, but CentOS 8 ships with Lua 5.3.)",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2021-03-10T13:29:31.734Z",
